      {
        "question_text": "Write these recurring decimals using dot notation.\n(a) $2.666666\\ldots$\n(b) $4.833333\\ldots$",
        "solution_text": "(a) The digit $6$ repeats.\n$2.666666\\ldots=2.\\dot{6}$\n(b) The $8$ appears once; the digit $3$ repeats.\n$4.833333\\ldots=4.8\\dot{3}$"
      },
      {
        "question_text": "Write these recurring decimals using both bar notation and dots over the first and last repeating digits.\n(a) $5.274274274\\ldots$\n(b) $6.0327327327\\ldots$",
        "solution_text": "(a) The block $274$ repeats.\n$\\begin{aligned}&\\mathrel{\\phantom{=}}5.274274274\\ldots\\\\&=5.\\overline{274}\\\\&=5.\\dot{2}7\\dot{4}\\end{aligned}$\nThe middle digit $7$ repeats too.\n(b) The first decimal digit $0$ does not repeat; the block $327$ repeats after it.\n$\\begin{aligned}&\\mathrel{\\phantom{=}}6.0327327327\\ldots\\\\&=6.0\\overline{327}\\\\&=6.0\\dot{3}2\\dot{7}\\end{aligned}$\nKeep the non-repeating zero unmarked."
      }
    ],
